  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Cp Wholesale India Private Limited & Anr vs State Govt.Of Nct Of Delhi & Ors on 14 July, 2022 Author: Asha Menon Bench: Asha Menon $~44 * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi + W.P.(Crl) 1515/2022, Crl.M.A.13234/2022 (for stay) Cp Wholesale India Private Limited & Anr. ..... Pe Through: Ms. Shweta Bharti, Mr. Anil Ti Mr. Aayushya Aankul and Mr. Aeshwarya Sisodia, Advocates versus State Govt.Of Nct Of Delhi & Ors. ..... Responde Through: Ms. Nandita Rao, Asc (Crl) for State (Gnctd) with Mr. Amit Peswani, Advocate Mr. Abhishek Singh, Mr. J. Amal Anand, Mr. Elvin Joshy and Ms. Alisha Sharma, Advocates for R-3 and R-7 Coram: Hon'Ble Ms. Justice Asha Menon Order % 14.07.2022 Crl.M.A.13233/2022 (Exemption)",
    "facts": "1 3. It is submitted that though petitioners have always purchased their ghee from respondent No.3/ M/s Gujarat Co-operative Milk Marketing Federation Ltd. (Amul) but the Batch, the number of which was of the product that was found to be sub-standard, was never purchased by them. As such, there was nothing to connect the sub-standard item with the petitioners.",
    "arguments": "2. It is submitted by Ms. Shweta Bharti, learned counsel for the petitioner that they have nothing to do with the sale of the ghee that was found to be sub-standard by the Food Safety Officer and therefore the complaint ought to be [LEAKAGE_MASK] qua them.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. It is submitted by Ms. Shweta Bharti, learned counsel for the petitioner that they have nothing to do with the sale of the ghee that was found to be sub-standard by the Food Safety Officer and therefore the complaint ought to be [LEAKAGE_MASK] qua them.",
